{
  "title": "mcu_power",
  "summary": "Battery, power switch, low-noise analog LDO and the XIAO nRF52840 on one page. 1S protected LiPo on J1 (JST PH). SW1 is the main power switch in the battery line: off disconnects everything, so charging through the XIAO also needs SW1 on. After the switch the cell (VBAT) goes to the MCU page, where the charge-link jumper feeds the XIAO, and to U1. U1 (TPS7A2033, 7 uVrms) makes the partners' +3.3V analog rail directly from the cell; its EN has an internal 500k pulldown, so the analog side stays off until the MCU drives ANA_EN high. No boost converter anywhere: the LDO holds 3.3 V until the cell is near empty. U1 is a Seeed XIAO nRF52840, soldered by its castellated edge pads; the only underside pad used is VBAT (solder through a plated hole from the back). SPI to the ADS131M08 is on the XIAO's default SPI pins D8/D9/D10 with 33 ohm series resistors to slow the edges near the analog front end. D7 = CS, D6 = DRDY (interrupt), D5 = SYNC/RESET (pulled up so the ADC is not held in reset while the XIAO boots), D4 = ANA_EN for the analog LDO. The ADC master clock defaults to 8 MHz from D3 through R5; Y1 (8.192 MHz oscillator) with R6 and C1 is an unfitted alternative: fit Y1, C1, R6 and remove R5 to switch. D0-D2 (analog-capable) are spare. VBUS sensing needs no pin: VBUS reaches the nRF inside the module. FIRMWARE NOTE: when ANA_EN is low the ADC is unpowered, so drive every ADC-facing pin low or high-Z first, or the ADC back-powers through its input diodes.",
